  "solution": {
    "text": "Feldspars are a group of rock-forming tectosilicate minerals. <br/>Mica minerals are phyllosilicate compounds. <br/>Zeolites are a large group of minerals consisting of hydrated aluminosilicates of Sodium, Potassium, Calcium and Barium. <br/>Thus, it is evident that Silicates are the basic component in Feldspars, Mica, Zeolites and Asbestos and have <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> basic unit.",
